  "title": "G-Helper: Control Tool for ASUS windows",
  "date": "2026-06-23T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "G-Helper: Control Tool for ASUS windows\n\nI downgraded my Windows 11 to Windows 10. I still have a lot software that can not run in Linux, but windows 11 is just too slow.\n\nHowever, as long as I plug in, the fan runs crazily. Even though, it is the balance mode.\n\nThen I found G-Helper, it can force the laptop into silent mode even it is plugged in.\n\nscreenshot\n\nI strongly suggest every ASUS user to try it.",
